-- title:
--   Rosenlicht generation of the glued degree-zero class group
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field and $F$ a field extension of $K$ which is a curve over $K$ in the sense of `IsCurveOver`: every nonzero $f \in F$ has a principal divisor of degree zero (the divisor $v \mapsto v.\mathrm{ord}\,f$), each place has residue field finite over $K$, and $\Omega[F/K]$ is free of rank one over $F$. Here places are valuation subrings of $F$ containing $K$, proper and with principal ideals, and $\mathrm{Divisor}\,K\,F$ is the group of finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued functions on places, with $\deg$ weighting each place by its residue degree. Assume given a divisor $K_C$ and $g \in \mathbb{N}$ such that $\ell(D) - \ell(K_C - D) = \deg D + 1 - g$ for every divisor $D$, where $\ell(D)$ is the $K$-dimension of the Riemann–Roch space of $D$, and assume the set of places is infinite. Let $S$ be a finite set of pairs of places whose members are determined by their second coordinate (any two elements of $S$ with the same second coordinate coincide), and let $E_1$, $E_2$ be finite sets of places containing all first, respectively second, coordinates of members of $S$. The group $\mathrm{GluedPic0}\,K\,F\,S$ is the quotient of the admissible gluing data — triples $(D_1, D_2, w)$ with $D_1, D_2$ of degree zero, $D_1$ vanishing at every first coordinate and $D_2$ at every second coordinate of members of $S$, and $w : S \to \mathrm{Additive}\,K^\times$ — by the subgroup `GluingData.gluedPrincipal S` of glued principal data. The assertion is that every $c$ in this quotient lies in the additive subgroup generated by the classes of those admissible data which, for some places $P, Q$, equal either $([P] - [Q], 0, 0)$ with $P, Q \notin E_1$, or $(0, [P] - [Q], 0)$ with $P, Q \notin E_2$ (the last coordinate being the trivial gluing unit).
--
--   This is the generation statement for the generalised Jacobian of the curve obtained by gluing two copies of a curve along the pairs in $S$: such a glued degree-zero class group is generated by differences of two places on a single copy, with the places avoidable outside any prescribed finite set. It is used to determine homomorphisms out of the special fibre of the Néron model of $J_H$ by their values on differences of liftable smooth points, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.mem_closure_gluedPic0_mk_configuredPair`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.mem_closure_gluedPic0_mk_configuredPair).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_GluedPic0_mem_closure_mk_pair_of_riemannRoch.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_AdelicIndex
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_GluedPic0

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u v

open AlgebraicCurve

theorem AlgebraicCurve.GluedPic0.mem_closure_mk_pair_of_riemannRoch
    {K : Type u} {F : Type v} [Field K] [Field F] [Algebra K F] [IsAlgClosed K]
    [IsCurveOver K F] (Kc : Divisor K F) (g : ℕ)
    (hRR : ∀ D : Divisor K F, (ell D : ℤ) - ell (Kc - D) = Divisor.degree D + 1 - g)
    [Infinite (Place K F)]
    (S : Finset (Place K F × Place K F)) (hS : ∀ s ∈ S, ∀ s' ∈ S, s.2 = s'.2 → s = s')
    (E₁ E₂ : Finset (Place K F)) (hE₁ : ∀ s ∈ S, s.1 ∈ E₁) (hE₂ : ∀ s ∈ S, s.2 ∈ E₂)
    (c : GluedPic0 K F S) :
    c ∈ AddSubgroup.closure {c | ∃ (P Q : Place K F) (x : ↥(GluingData.admissible S)),
        ((P ∉ E₁ ∧ Q ∉ E₁ ∧ (x : GluingData K F S) = (Finsupp.single P 1 - Finsupp.single Q 1, 0, 0)) ∨
         (P ∉ E₂ ∧ Q ∉ E₂ ∧ (x : GluingData K F S) = (0, Finsupp.single P 1 - Finsupp.single Q 1, 0))) ∧
        c = GluedPic0.mk S x} := by sorry
